    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Shaka turned the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zulu-kingdom">Zulu</a> from a small regional <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chiefdom">chiefdom</a> into the leading power of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, ruling over 250,000 people and able to muster more than 50,000 warriors by his death in 1828.</li><li>He is credited with the iklwa stabbing spear, the &quot;bull horn&quot; formation and the age-grade regiments, though scholars dispute how far these were his inventions and how far he drew on existing practice.</li><li>His reign brought a massive number of deaths and coincided with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mfecane">Mfecane</a>, and how far he was to blame, and how far his image as a monster was made by European traders and later historians, is still argued.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Shaka's name is roughly translated as &quot;intestinal beetle&quot;.</p></aside>
    </section>

